Description: Implements the Simple Non-Iterative Clustering (SNIC) algorithm 
    for superpixel segmentation of multi-band images, as introduced by Achanta 
    and Süsstrunk (2017) <doi:10.1109/CVPR.2017.520>. Supports both standard 
    image arrays and geospatial raster objects (currently via the terra 
    package), with a design that can be extended to other spatial data 
    frameworks. SNIC rapidly groups adjacent pixels into compact, coherent 
    regions ("superpixels") based on spectral similarity and spatial 
    proximity. This high-performance C++ implementation supports images 
    with arbitrary spectral bands and is exposed to R via a small interface. 
    The main function snic() returns objects of class "snic", which bundle 
    the labels with per-segment summaries and centroids. 
